{"type":"message","id":"51a92148","parentId":"cd0ed4b4","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:51:43.062Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`. It used `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")`, a fixed format with nothing to match a trailing `Z`, so that letter was left over and raised the error. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass: `test_dates`, `test_naive` and `test_day_key`.\n\nTwo behaviour changes:\n- **Time zones are kept now.** A string ending in `Z` returns a datetime marked as UTC, and one with an offset like `+02:00` keeps that offset. Strings with no zone still return a datetime with no zone, as before. Comparing a zoned datetime with an unzoned one raises `TypeError`, so any caller that mixes the two would break.\n- **It accepts more ISO-8601 forms than before**, such as fractional seconds or date-only strings.\n\n`fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 or newer. The local Python is 3.13.5, and the repo has no `pyproject.toml` or `setup.py` stating a minimum version. On Python 3.10 or older, `Z` input would fail again."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":404,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":26848,"totalTokens":27254,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":26848}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277498470,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dRPQNgRz7KMEeXtQup","duration":4590.816395000002,"ttft":4565.036877999999,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26850,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
